* t45seek.a -- CONF68K test t45: I$Seek on an SCF (character device) path.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): I$Seek is not a valid service request for SCF, and* SCF does NOT return an error for it. The manual states both halves in the* same place: the list of requests "not valid for SCF" contains I$Seek, and* the sentence after it says an error IS returned for I$ChgDir, I$Delete and* I$MakDir but that I$Seek does not return one. I$Seek's own entry states the* general rule the same way -- managers without random access do nothing and* return no error -- and names SBF as the manager that errors instead.** The distinction this test has to respect: "does not return an error" is the* whole claim. SCF has no position to inspect afterwards, so a test asserting* that the seek also did NOTHING would be asserting something the interface* cannot show. This checks only what the manual states.** /term is opened explicitly rather than seeking a standard path, and that is* load-bearing: under runall path 1 is redirected into RESULTS/report, which* is an RBF file where I$Seek is perfectly valid, so a test seeking it would* pass on any system whatever SCF did. A system with no /term reports ERROR* here, which is the documented meaning -- the test could not set up the* situation it meant to check.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1IOpen set $84ISeek set $88IClose set $8F*EXPECT set 0* psect t45seek,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,2048,startstart lea tname(pc),a0 moveq #1,d0 trap #0 dc.w IOpen bcs.w setuperr move.w d0,d7* the call under test moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 moveq #0,d1 trap #0 dc.w ISeek bcc.s t45ok moveq #0,d6 move.w d1,d6 bra.s t45clst45ok moveq #0,d6t45cls moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IClose cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.s ispass bra.s isfail* use verdict.i use report.i*tname dc.b "/term",0idstr dc.b "RESULT t45 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  I$Seek on an SCF path does not return an error",0 ends